    # v400 (24/10/2026) -- ERRATUM BESIDE the v399 section (the redeclared alpha and the beta check). The text is fixed; the embedded-block hash and the relative beta difference ARE READ from the selo_pela_propria_tecnologia_v399 record, never typed.
    # The box at the top (The Test of the Only Word, v397) stays where it is: the 4.44 rule is not touched. Nothing here moves the gate.
    _sv400 = (core.get("selo_pela_propria_tecnologia_v399") or {}).get("values") or {}
    _h400 = lambda x_: (r"\texttt{" + x_[:16] + "}") if isinstance(x_, str) and len(x_) >= 16 else r"\text{n/a}"
    _e400 = lambda x_: (r"\texttt{" + ("%.1e" % x_) + "}") if isinstance(x_, float) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    s.append(r"\textbf{Erratum beside it (v400).} \textsf{[REAL]} The section above describes sealing by its own technology as v399 sealed it, and v399 carried an integration defect that the Bancada Um pointed out when trying to synchronise it: "
             r"the seal adaptation (the management's code, before the operator's block) \emph{redeclared} the literal of $\alpha$ on a non-indented line of \texttt{um.py}, and the Bancada's synchronisation sketch requires a single $\alpha$ line in the program (\texttt{ALPHA\_LINHA\_NAO\_UNICA}). "
             r"The refusal closed as it should (fail-closed): v399 stays sealed as it is, and the Bancada's next step is v400. v400 fixes it without adding anything to the kernel or to the records: the section now \emph{reads} the program's own $\alpha$ (\texttt{SEALED\_CODATA\_ALPHA}), "
             r"so the program has a single declaration of $\alpha$ and no literal of $\beta$ ($\beta=\alpha\sqrt{e}$ at run time, never literal); the operator's block (hash " + _h400(_sv400.get("bloco_embutido_sha256")) + r") does not change, nor does the profile, the negative controls or the sidecar. "
             r"And the ``$\beta$ of the runtime'' check of the seal record, which compared the computed $\beta$ with the same $\alpha\sqrt{e}$ (tautological), now confronts the $\beta$ of the rite's core: relative difference measured in this rite " + _e400(_sv400.get("rel_beta_vs_core")) + r", tolerance $10^{-9}$. "
             r"No stone, no new record, no new inscription; validity in the kernel is not accreditation and the gate does not move. The box ``The Test of the Only Word'' stays at the top, with its $5\sigma$ line.")
